Similar to the {{w|Compound eye|compound vision}} of an insect, Eye Guy's eyes give him 360-degree vision,{{Refn|Eye Guy's vision was first portrayed on-screen as all green,<ref name="Rad" /> before being different later on.<ref name="SZTWC" />|group = note}} making it extremely difficult to sneak up on him.<ref name="B10vN102">''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 2]]''</ref> The eyes on his hands further allow him to peer around corners or obstacles.{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = link}}<ref name="WXI2"/> Furthermore, he can "smell" and see trails of certain chemicals with his eyes, as shown when he was able to see the trail of [[Ignacius Baumann|Mr. Baumann]]'s cologne.<ref name="BoMB">''[[The Ballad of Mr. Baumann]]''</ref>

Eye Guy has ophthalmokinesis, which allows him to control and alter the many eyes on his body. He can move his eyes across the surface of his body and merge them together to create one bigger eye.<ref name="B10vN102"/> By closing all his other eyes,{{Refn|In the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''', Eye Guy was able to freely fire both charged and uncharged blasts from his chest eye without affecting his other eyes; the only exception being when he brought the chest eye out on a stalk, which retracted all of the other eyes on his body.<ref name="SotO">'''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix]]''''' <small>(Gold Edition)</small></ref> As of '''Omniverse''', Eye Guy always closes all his other eyes to open and fire from his chest eye.|group = note}} he can open his chest eye and further bring it out on a stalk to point it around.<ref name="BoMB" />

From any of the eyes on his torso, and from multiple at once,<ref name="UVT" /> Eye Guy can fire out green{{Refn|Alternate versions of Eye Guy are shown firing optic blasts in different colors. For example, [[Ben_23|Ben 23]]'s [[Eye Guy (Dimension 23)|Eye Guy]] fires blue blasts<ref>''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref> while [[Weapon XI (Flashback)|Weapon XI]] fired red blasts.<ref name="WXI2">''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]''</ref>|group = note}} optic blasts.{{Refn|[[:File:EyeGuy prompt and development.png]]|group = TNP|name = prompt}} These beams of energy can easily push objects or people far away;<ref name="B10vN102"/><ref name="WXI2"/> give enough kickback for Eye Guy to launch himself in the air;<ref name="Mud">''[[Mud is Thicker Than Water]]''</ref> and are powerful enough to shatter metal<ref name="Mud"/> and slice trees clean in half, the latter demonstrated by [[Weapon XI (Flashback)|Weapon XI]].<ref name="WXI2"/> Eye Guy's chest eye can charge up and fire larger and more powerful beams of super concentrated energy.{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = link}} These beams are capable of shattering [[Rock Monster]]s in one shot<ref>''[[Mystery, Incorporeal]]''</ref> and, if sustained, can ignite an explosive barrel and overload machinery.<ref name="SotO" />

The eyes all over Eye Guy's body can each fire a different kind of optic blast:{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = link}} Besides simple energy beams, he can shoot blasts of green fire;<ref name="TUH">''[[The Ultimate Heist]]''</ref> green freeze rays that encase and immobilize a target in ice on contact;<ref name="Mud"/> green bolts of electricity;<ref name="SotO" /><ref name="B10vN102"/> green bolts of electricity capable of freezing foes such as [[Clancy]];<ref name="B10vN102"/> and blasts of sticky eye goop.{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = link}}

Eye Guy has enhanced durability, being able to take punches from the [[Galactic Gladiator]],<ref name="UVT">''[[Universe vs. Tennyson]]''</ref> and an energy blast from the [[Mutant Giraffe]] directly to the face.<ref name="EE">''[[Evil's Encore]]''</ref>

Eye Guy is capable of performing great acrobatic and gymnastic feats, as well as jumping several feet high.<ref name="SotO" /><ref name="Mud" />

Eye Guy has good reflexes, capable of dodging incoming attacks.<ref name="IaMMMBW2" />

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow" position="right">
RadEp (209).png|Physical Eye Damage
BoB (117).png|Eye Irritation
SZTWC (593).png|Amplified Phobias
</gallery>
If an irritant such as [[Gracklflint]] venom gets in his eyes, Eye Guy's eyes will burn and he will briefly be unable to see clearly. Because he has eyes over the majority of his body, he is more vulnerable to being exposed to and hurt by such irritants.<ref name="Rad">''[[Rad]]''</ref>

Certain chemicals can irritate Eye Guy's eyes and cause them to tear up, such as [[Ignacius Baumann|Mr. Baumann]]'s cologne.<ref name="BoMB" />

Eye Guy's multiplied vision can be a weakness to the person transformed as him; if they look at something or someone that they have a fear of, like [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]], they will now see multiple of that and become more frightened than normal.<ref name="SZTWC">''[[Something Zombozo This Way Comes]]''</ref>

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Eye Guy was unlocked off-screen prior to ''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 1]]''.
*Eye Guy first appeared in ''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 2]]'', where he battled the [[Negative 10]].
*In the Gold Edition of '''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix]]''''', Eye Guy fought a [[Mutant Wasp]] and destroyed [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s [[Devolution Bomb|DNA bomb]], accidentally activating the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]]'s Self-Destruct Mode in the process.

===Five Years Prior to Omniverse===
*In ''[[Evil's Encore]]'', Eye Guy battled [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]] and his [[Mutant Giraffe]], but failed to defeat them when he reverted.
*In ''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]'', Eye Guy was defeated by [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] when he [[Weapon XI (Flashback)|absorbed some power]] from the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]].
*In ''[[From Hedorium to Eternity]]'', Eye Guy defeated a [[Ectonurite (Classic)|possessed]] [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]].

===Alien Force=== 
*Eye Guy was removed from the active playlist by the Omnitrix's reconfiguration in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''.

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Eye Guy was re-unlocked by [[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|Ben 10,000]].

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Rad]]'', Eye Guy was defeated by the [[Gracklflint]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', Eye Guy appeared before [[Blukic]] and [[Driba]]. Later, Eye Guy battled [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Ultimate Humungousaur]], but was defeated by Negative [[Ultimate Echo Echo]].
*In ''[[Mud is Thicker Than Water]]'', Eye Guy helped [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] stabilize the power core of the [[Plumber Headquarters|Plumber Headquarters]].
*In ''[[A Fistful of Brains]]'', Eye Guy was defeated by [[Ultimate Albedo]].
*In ''[[Something Zombozo This Way Comes]]'', Eye Guy was frightened by [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]] and accidentally switched himself into [[Toepick]].
*In ''[[Mystery, Incorporeal]]'', Eye Guy battled some [[Rock Monster]]s.
*In ''[[Universe vs. Tennyson]]'', Eye Guy was defeated by the [[Galactic Gladiator]].
*In ''[[Charm School]]'', Eye Guy looked for [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]] in the campus of [[Friedkin University]] before being scared by Gwen.
*In ''[[The Ballad of Mr. Baumann]]'', Eye Guy followed [[Ignacius Baumann|Mr. Baumann]]'s cologne trail to find him and [[Sheelane]].
*In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]'', Eye Guy defeated [[Mad Rook]] with the help of [[Freeze-Ghost]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Eye Guy appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

